    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "The Just Judgment of the Wicked"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "To the Chief Musician. Set to “Do Not Destroy.” A Michtam of David."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Do you indeed speak righteousness, you silent ones?",
          "Do you judge uprightly, you sons of men?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "No, in heart you work wickedness;",
          "You weigh out the violence of your hands in the earth."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The wicked are estranged from the womb;",
          "They go astray as soon as they are born, speaking lies."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Their poison is like the poison of a serpent;",
          "They are like the deaf cobra that stops its ear,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Which will not heed the voice of charmers,",
          "Charming ever so skillfully."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Break their teeth in their mouth, O God!",
          "Break out the fangs of the young lions, O Lord!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let them flow away as waters which run continually;",
          "When he bends his bow,",
          "Let his arrows be as if cut in pieces."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let them be like a snail which melts away as it goes,",
          "Like a stillborn child of a woman, that they may not see the sun."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Before your pots can feel the burning thorns,",
          "He shall take them away as with a whirlwind,",
          "As in His living and burning wrath."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The righteous shall rejoice when he sees the vengeance;",
          "He shall wash his feet in the blood of the wicked,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "So that men will say,",
          "“Surely there is a reward for the righteous;",
          "Surely He is God who judges in the earth.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
